    chapter("achievements", "RetroAchievements", "Sign-in, API sync, library badges and achievement artwork",
        topic("Sign in and enable tracking", "Open RetroAchievements while connected to the internet and sign in. Enable RetroAchievements permits tracking; disabling it is useful for testing and preserves the stored login/library data. Re-enable before a fresh game launch to resume normal tracking. Do not share passwords or API keys in bug reports."),
        topic("Sync the scanned library", "Scan your game library first. In RetroAchievements → Library progress, use RetroAchievements control panel to visit the account website while signed in. Find Keys, copy the Web API key into the app's separate Web API key field, then run Sync library. Username/password sign-in does not fill that key. Manual sync reads/hashes images, so large libraries and Android document storage can take time."),
        topic("Matched games and missing hashes", "After syncing, open the RetroAchievements library list and select a matched game to view its achievements and artwork outside gameplay. Matched does not mean already played: a supported unplayed game can show 0/total. Unmatched, unreadable or unsupported images need checking separately; do not assume a title-only match proves the disc hash is supported."),
        topic("Library achievement badges", "Supported/synced games can show achievement availability/progress in list, grid and shelf views, including PS one styling. A badge uses cached progress and may need syncing after play. Achievement art needs network access on first retrieval. Games without a matched set should not acquire a badge merely because their title resembles a supported release."),
        topic("Hardcore support", "This SwanStation integration does not currently enable Hardcore mode. A frontend label or old stored preference is not proof that Hardcore validation is active. Use the supported tracking features; do not rely on this build for verified Hardcore awards."),
