    chapter("appearance", "App appearance and interface", "Themes, music, scaling and launcher preferences",
        topic("Original ARMSX1 and PS one styles", "Open Sidebar → Options → Customisation → Interface style and select Original ARMSX1 or PS one. Original keeps the normal frontend style; PS one changes the library/menu shell and controls. Colour themes and wallpapers are separate preferences. These controls are no longer in Settings → App. These change the app interface, not the game's emulated console or textures."),
        topic("Colours, wallpaper and backgrounds", "Open Sidebar → Options → Customisation. Expand Theme for the colour scheme, including system/Material You, custom colours and OLED base where offered. PS one uses its own fixed palette; return Interface style to Original ARMSX1 to choose colour themes. Expand Background style to choose the original waves, PS one background or a custom image, and adjust wave colours, RGB cycling or simple 2D animation where offered. These controls were moved out of Settings → App without resetting saved values or deleting images. The dropdowns start collapsed and can be opened independently. Touch-control skins change button artwork separately from the library/menu appearance."),
        topic("Library and pause music", "Enable each music source separately, choose a custom file or restore the default, and adjust its own volume. Menu sound effects can use short clips in a selected folder named for events such as nav, select, submenu, menu, back, toggle_on, toggle_off, reset, slider, sleep and wake. Use supported audio formats and keep effect clips short."),
        topic("Toolbar, search, recents and keyboard", "Choose top/bottom toolbar placement in App settings. Toggle the search field and Recently Played independently. Adjust cover size, tile opacity and grid names for readability. Enable System keyboard if you prefer Android's IME; the built-in keyboard remains available for controller-driven entry."),
        topic("Interface size and font size", "Settings → Interface changes UI size and text size, not the internal game resolution. Start with moderate values and check both orientations. Larger text can wrap into additional lines; use a smaller overall UI scale if controls no longer fit. The manual follows the app theme and text sizing."),
        topic("Boot logo, activity sharing and Home behaviour", "The boot-logo switch changes the app startup presentation. Recent-game/activity sharing belongs to the social features, not the public cheat database. Home-blocking changes navigation behaviour while the app is active and cannot replace Android system permissions. Use the option descriptions to decide whether these preferences suit your device."),
