    chapter("troubleshooting", "Troubleshooting", "Fast checks before resetting or deleting data",
        topic("Game missing or file inaccessible", "Refresh the library, check the active search/collection/hidden filters, confirm the folder permission and verify the file still exists. For CUE, grant the containing folder and inspect track filenames. A ROM on cloud storage may not be locally readable yet. Changing video settings cannot repair a missing file."),
        topic("Slowdown or stutter", "Return to 100% speed with the normal limiter. Disable runahead, heavy shaders and texture dumping, then try a lower internal resolution. Compare the same scene in another supported renderer and watch heat/frame-time readings. Restore settings one at a time; avoid globally resetting games that already work."),
        topic("Picture sideways, cropped or too large", "Check Launcher orientation, Gameplay orientation and Display rotation independently. Return overscan to None and compare the normal aspect ratio, stretch and integer-scaling settings. A dual-screen handheld's display orientation can differ from a phone's. Relaunch after a renderer/driver change."),
        topic("Audio delayed or crackling", "Test ordinary speed without fast-forward, verify full-speed emulation, then compare offered audio buffers/backends. Try low-volume speakers and wired headphones to separate speaker distortion from emulation problems. Bluetooth introduces its own delay. Describe whether the fault is only BIOS audio or also present in gameplay."),
        topic("Settings or controls seem not to save", "Verify Global/This game scope, the active control profile and any per-game override. Relaunch for startup-only settings. A separate test app has separate preferences. An import/reset may replace your chosen values, so keep a backup and test an ordinary edit before deleting profiles."),
